 thesis."}}],"narrative":[],"overrides_applied":[]},"nodes":[{"id":"C&EE M20","title":"Introduction to Computer Programming with MATLAB","units":"4","offered":["Fall"],"level":"lower","status":"active","in_major":true,"role":"required","groups":["Preparation for the Major: Earth, Planetary, and Space Sciences M71 Substitution"],"column":1,"prereq_text":"Mathematics 33A","requires":{"type":"course","code":"MATH 33A","concurrent":false,"min_grade":null},"ambiguous":false,"description":"(Same as Mechanical and Aerospace Engineering M20.) Lecture, two hours; discussion, two hours; laboratory, two hours; outside study, six hours. Fundamentals of computer programming taught in context of MATLAB computing environment. Basic data types and control structures. Input/output. Functions. Data visualization. MATLAB-based data structures. Development of efficient codes. Introduction to object-oriented programming. Examples and exercises from engineering, mathematics, and physical sciences. Letter grading.","url":"https://catalog.registrar.ucla.edu/course/2026/CEEM20"},{"id":"CHEM 14A","title":"General Chemistry for Life Scientists I","units":"4","offered":[],"level":"lower","status":"active","in_major":true,"role":"choice","groups":["Preparation for the Major: Chemistry 14 series"],"column":0,"prereq_text":"completion of Chemistry Diagnostic Test; and (Life Sciences 30A or Mathematics 3A or 31A or score of 48 or better on Mathematics Diagnostic Test) (may be taken concurrently)","requires":{"type":"and","items":[{"type":"condition","kind":"other","text":"completion of Chemistry Diagnostic Test"},{"type":"or","items":[{"type":"course","code":"LIFESCI 30A","concurrent":true,"min_grade":null},{"type":"course","code":"MATH 3A","concurrent":true,"min_grade":null},{"type":"course","code":"MATH 31A","concurrent":true,"min_grade":null},{"type":"condition","kind":"other","text":"score of 48"}]}]},"ambiguous":false,"description":"Lecture, three hours; discussion, one hour. Preparation: high school chemistry or equivalent background and three and one half years of high school mathematics. Not open to students with credit for course 20A. Introduction to physical and general chemistry principles; atomic structure based on quantum mechanics; atomic properties; trends in periodic table; chemical bonding (Lewis structures, VSEPR theory, hybridization, and molecular orbital theory); coordination compounds; properties of inorganic and organic acids, bases, buffers. P/NP or letter grading.","url":"https://catalog.registrar.ucla.edu/course/2026/CHEM14A"},{"id":"CHEM 14AE","title":"General Chemistry for Life Scientists I—Enhanced","units":"4","offered":[],"level":"lower","status":"active","in_major":false,"role":"prerequisite","groups":[],"column":0,"prereq_text":"completion of Chemistry Diagnostic Test; and (Life Sciences 30A or Mathematics 3A or 31A or score of 48 or better on Mathematics Diagnostic Test) (may be taken concurrently)","requires":{"type":"and","items":[{"type":"condition","kind":"other","text":"completion of Chemistry Diagnostic Test"},{"type":"or","items":[{"type":"course","code":"LIFESCI 30A","concurrent":true,"min_grade":null},{"type":"course","code":"MATH 3A","concurrent":true,"min_grade":null},{"type":"course","code":"MATH 31A","concurrent":true,"min_grade":null},{"type":"condition","kind":"other","text":"score of 48"}]}]},"ambiguous":false,"description":"Lecture, three hours; discussion, two hours. Preparation: high school chemistry or equivalent background and three and one half years of high school mathematics. Not open to students with credit for course 14A or 20A. Study of foundations of chemistry. Discussion of foundations of quantum mechanics and how these principles can be used to understand atomic and molecular structure and properties; how molecules interact; and properties of inorganic, organic, and biological acids, bases, and salts. Biological, environmental, and socially-relevant examples are used to illustrate central role that chemistry plays in our world. Emphasis on developing problem-solving skills and collaborative interaction and learning. P/NP or letter grading.","url":"https://catalog.registrar.ucla.edu/course/2026/CHEM14AE"},{"id":"CHEM 14B","title":"General Chemistry for Life Scientists II","units":"4","offered":[],"level":"lower","status":"active","in_major":true,"role":"choice","groups":["Preparation for the Major: Chemistry 14 series"],"column":0,"prereq_text":"one course from 14A, 14AE, 20A, or 20AH with grade of C– or better; and (Life Sciences 30B or Mathematics 3B or 31B with grade of C– or better) (may be taken concurrently)","requires":{"type":"and","items":[{"type":"condition","kind":"other","text":"one course from 14A"},{"type":"or","items":[{"type":"course","code":"LIFESCI 30B","concurrent":true,"min_grade":"C-"},{"type":"course","code":"MATH 3B","concurrent":true,"min_grade":"C-"},{"type":"course","code":"MATH 31B","concurrent":true,"min_grade":"C-"}]}]},"ambiguous":false,"description":"Lecture, three hours; discussion, one hour. Enforced requisite or Not open to students with credit for course 14BE, 20B, or 20BH. Chemical equilibria in gases and liquids, acid-base equilibrium; phase changes; thermochemistry; first, second, and third laws of thermodynamics; free energy changes; electrochemistry and its role as energy source; chemical kinetics, including catalysis, and reaction mechanisms. P/NP or letter grading.","url":"https://catalog.registrar.ucla.edu/course/2026/CHEM14B"},{"id":"CHEM 14BL","title":"General and Organic Chemistry Laboratory I","units":"3","offered":[],"level":"lower","status":"active","in_major":true,"role":"choice","groups":["Preparation for the Major: Chemistry 14 series"],"column":1,"prereq_text":"course 14A or 20A or 20AH with grade of C– or better; and (course 14B) (may be taken concurrently)","requires":{"type":"and","items":[{"type":"or","items":[{"type":"course","code":"CHEM 14A","concurrent":false,"min_grade":"C-"},{"type":"course","code":"CHEM 20A","concurrent":false,"min_grade":"C-"},{"type":"course","code":"CHEM 20AH","concurrent":false,"min_grade":"C-"}]},{"type":"course","code":"CHEM 14B","concurrent":true,"min_grade":null}]},"ambiguous":false,"description":"Lecture, one hour; laboratory, three hours. Not open to students with credit for course 20L. Introduction to volumetric, spectrophotometric, and potentiometric analysis. Use and preparation of buffers and pH meters. Synthesis and kinetics techniques using compounds of interest to students in life sciences. P/NP or letter grading.","url":"https://catalog.registrar.ucla.edu/course/2026/CHEM14BL"},{"id":"CHEM 20A","title":"Chemical Structure","units":"4","offered":[],"level":"lower","status":"active","in_major":true,"role":"choice","groups":["Preparation for the Major: Chemistry 20 series"],"column":0,"prereq_text":"completion of Chemistry Diagnostic Test; and (Mathematics 31A) (may be taken concurrently)","requires":{"type":"and","items":[{"type":"condition","kind":"other","text":"completion of Chemistry Diagnostic Test"},{"type":"course","code":"MATH 31A","concurrent":true,"min_grade":null}]},"ambiguous":false,"description":"Lecture, three hours; discussion, one hour. Preparation: high school chemistry or equivalent background and three and one half years of high school mathematics. Not open to students with credit for course 14A. First term of general chemistry. Survey of chemical processes, quantum chemistry, atomic and molecular structure and bonding, molecular spectroscopy. P/NP or letter grading.","url":"https://catalog.registrar.ucla.edu/course/2026/CHEM20A"},{"id":"CHEM 20AH","title":"Chemical Structure (Honors)","units":"4","offered":[],"level":"lower","status":"active","in_major":false,"role":"prerequisite","groups":[],"column":0,"prereq_text":"(Mathematics 31A) (may be taken concurrently)","requires":{"type":"course","code":"MATH 31A","concurrent":true,"min_grade":null},"ambiguous":false,"description":"Lecture, three hours; discussion, one hour. Preparation: high school chemistry or equivalent background, high school physics, and three and one half years of high school mathematics. Honors course parallel to course 20A. P/NP or letter grading.","url":"https://catalog.registrar.ucla.edu/course/2026/CHEM20AH"},{"id":"CHEM 20B","title":"Chemical Energetics and Change","units":"4","offered":[],"level":"lower","status":"active","in_major":true,"role":"choice","groups":["Preparation for the Major: Chemistry 20 series"],"column":1,"prereq_text":"course 14A or 14AE or 20A or 20AH, and Mathematics 31A, with grades of C– or better; and (Mathematics 31B) (may be taken concurrently)","requires":{"type":"and","items":[{"type":"or","items":[{"type":"course","code":"CHEM 14A","concurrent":false,"min_grade":"C-"},{"type":"course","code":"CHEM 14AE","concurrent":false,"min_grade":"C-"},{"type":"course","code":"CHEM 20A","concurrent":false,"min_grade":"C-"},{"type":"course","code":"CHEM 20AH","concurrent":false,"min_grade":"C-"}]},{"type":"course","code":"MATH 31A","concurrent":false,"min_grade":"C-"},{"type":"course","code":"MATH 31B","concurrent":true,"min_grade":null}]},"ambiguous":false,"description":"Lecture, three hours; discussion, one hour. Second term of general chemistry. Intermolecular forces and organization, phase behavior, chemical thermodynamics, solutions, equilibria, reaction rates and laws. P/NP or letter grading.","url":"https://catalog.registrar.ucla.edu/course/2026/CHEM20B"},{"id":"CHEM 20L","title":"General Chemistry Laboratory","units":"3","offered":[],"level":"lower","status":"active","in_major":true,"role":"choice","groups":["Preparation for the Major: Chemistry 20 series"],"column":1,"prereq_text":"course 14A or 20A with grade of C– or better; and (course 14B or 20B) (may be taken concurrently)","requires":{"type":"and","items":[{"type":"or","items":[{"type":"course","code":"CHEM 14A","concurrent":false,"min_grade":"C-"},{"type":"course","code":"CHEM 20A","concurrent":false,"min_grade":"C-"}]},{"type":"or","items":[{"type":"course","code":"CHEM 14B","concurrent":true,"min_grade":null},{"type":"course","code":"CHEM 20B","concurrent":true,"min_grade":null}]}]},"ambiguous":false,"description":"Lecture, one hour; laboratory, three hours. Use of balance, volumetric techniques, volumetric and potentiometric analysis; Beer’s law, applications for environmental analysis and materials science. P/NP or letter grading.","url":"https://catalog.registrar.ucla.edu/course/2026/CHEM20L"},{"id":"CLUSTER 70A","title":"Evolution of Cosmos and Life","units":"6","offered":[],"level":"lower","status":"active","in_major":true,"role":"required","groups":["Preparation for the Major: Earth, Planetary, and Space Sciences 1 Substitution"],"column":0,"prereq_text":"","requires":null,"ambiguous":false,"description":"Lecture, three hours; discussion, two hours. Course 70A is enforced Limited to first-year freshmen. Use of concept of evolution, as it applies to biological organisms, Earth, solar system, and universe itself, to introduce students to both life and physical sciences. Examination of evolution of universe, galaxy, solar system, and Earth. P/NP or letter grading.","url":"https://catalog.registrar.ucla.edu/course/2026/CLUSTER70A"},{"id":"EPS SCI 1","title":"","units":"","offered":[],"level":"","status":"inactive","in_major":true,"role":"required","groups":["Preparation for the Major: Earth, Planetary, and Space Sciences"],"column":0,"prereq_text":"","requires":null,"ambiguous":false,"description":""},{"id":"EPS SCI 51","title":"","units":"","offered":[],"level":"","status":"inactive","in_major":true,"role":"required","groups":["Preparation for the Major: Earth, Planetary, and Space Sciences"],"column":0,"prereq_text":"","requires":null,"ambiguous":false,"description":""},{"id":"EPS SCI 61","title":"","units":"","offered":[],"level":"","status":"inactive","in_major":true,"role":"required","groups":["Preparation for the Major: Earth, Planetary, and Space Sciences"],"